- B | creep out of the hide and flush the bird up for a photograph | v: achievement, power | closed: approval: flushing a rare bird off a reserve; backfire: banned from the reserve, and named on every forum | chance: 50
- R | ring every friend you have from the hide, whispering at the top of your voice | v: stimulation, benevolence | tech: phone | chance: 80
- G | put the telescope down and watch the marsh until the bird walks into view | v: universalism (nature) | self_control: + | chance: 60
- W>B | volunteer as the reserve's warden, so the hide keys are yours | v: power | act: volunteer as the reserve's warden, so the hide keys are theirs | chance: 55
- U>R | work out where it will roost tonight, and be there alone at dusk | v: stimulation | chance: 60
- B>G | keep quiet about a second rare bird on the far pool, so the crowds stay away | v: universalism (nature) | chance: 80
- R>W | tell off the photographers creeping out onto the mud, loud enough for all | v: universalism, conformity | mark: made an enemy | chance: 50
- G>U | listen for its call among the curlews, as the old birders did before telescopes | v: self-direction, tradition | mark: learned a skill | chance: 70
works: The bird walks out from behind the dunlin into full view, and twenty people in the hide hold their breath at once.
works: {N} sees it for four seconds through the scope, clear as day, and goes home to write it in the book that holds forty years of birds.
fails: The flock lifts all at once and whirls away over the sea, and the bird is not seen again.
fails: A morning of frost and squinting, and it turns out the bird left the night before.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- elder: calls WB (cycle s3)

== the knitting circle at the library
tier: everyday
stages: elder
age: 60-100
calls: WB
tone: joy
life: community, friends, home
horizon: months
roles: rival, friend, sibling, a librarian
earth: the Wednesday knitting circle at the library, needles clicking, a pattern on the table and the county show coming up
times: Some older people, mostly women, most weeks for those in a group; most never join one (estimate)
gap: 2-4
rate: .5
# rate lowered (drafts/repeats/everyday.py)
scene: Eight chairs stand in a circle in the library's back room, with a tin of biscuits, a basket of wool ends and the steady click of needles under the talk. {N} has a half-made cardigan on the needles and a pattern on their knee.
scene W: Every winter the circle knits squares for blankets for the children's ward, and every square must be exactly eight inches or the blankets will not lie flat. {N} keeps the count.
scene U: The cable pattern on the chart is four symbols too clever for anyone in the room. {N} has a pencil, a magnifying glass and the whole afternoon.
scene B: The county show's knitting cup has gone to {rival} three years running. {N} has been studying that tension, and has a plan.
scene R: The whole circle knits in beige and lavender. {N} has a bag of wool in shocking orange and an idea that would make the librarian faint.
scene G: The needles were {Ns} mother's, the pattern came from a cousin, and the stitch goes back further than anyone in the family can remember.
- W | unpick any square that is not exactly eight inches, whoever knitted it | v: conformity | mark: made an enemy | closed: approval: unpicking other people's work; backfire: two of the circle walk out | chance: 80
- U | puzzle out the cable chart stitch by stitch, until the pattern comes | v: achievement, self-direction | mark: learned a skill | chance: 70
- B | study the champion's tension for months, and enter the show to beat them | v: achievement | mark: learned a skill | self_control: + | chance: 45
- R | cover the bench outside the town hall in orange knitting, one night | identity | v: stimulation, self-direction | mark: broke the law | closed: law: decorating public property without leave; backfire: the council cuts it off, and the paper asks who did it | chance: 80
- G | knit your mother's old pattern, slowly, and teach it to anyone who asks | identity | v: tradition | chance: 75
- W>R | start a lunchtime class for the teenagers from the school next door | door | v: benevolence | chance: 55
- U>G | work out the old stitch from a photograph of a grandmother's shawl | v: tradition, self-direction | chance: 65
- B>W | sell your best pieces at the craft fair and give the takings to the circle | v: benevolence, achievement | chance: 90
- R>U | throw away the pattern and knit whatever comes, just to see what happens | v: self-direction, stimulation | chance: 55
- G>B | let the gossip about the rival's shop-bought wool spread, and say nothing | v: power | mark: made an enemy | closed: approval: letting a rumour do the work; backfire: the rival finds out who started it | chance: 60
works: The cardigan comes off the needles perfect, and the circle passes it round like a newborn.
works: The show cup comes home to the circle at last, and there is cake on Wednesday.
fails: A dropped stitch twenty rows back, and the whole evening's work has to come undone.
fails: A row breaks out over the show, and two of the circle stop coming on Wednesdays.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- elder: calls UR (cycle s4)

== the camera club's theme of the month
tier: everyday
stages: elder
age: 60-95
calls: UR
tone: joy
life: nature, friends, play
horizon: week
roles: rival, child, friend, a judge at the club
earth: the camera club's theme this month is "water", the deadline is Friday, and the camera is still new
times: Uncommon: perhaps 1 in 30 older adults belong to a camera club, with a theme most months (estimate)
gap: 2-4
rate: .5
# rate lowered (drafts/repeats/everyday.py)
scene: The camera club's theme this month is "water", the deadline is Friday, and {N} stands on the harbour wall at dawn with a camera the family gave them for a big birthday, still learning what half the buttons do.
scene W: The club's rules are strict: one print, unaltered, with a title and the settings written on the back. {N} has read them twice.
scene U: Aperture, shutter speed, the way light bends on moving water: {N} has the manual open on the wall and wants to understand every number in it.
scene B: {rival} has won the monthly cup four times this year. {N} has a mind to take it away from them.
scene R: A wave smashes white against the harbour wall, and {N} wants to be closer, much closer, right in the spray with the camera.
scene G: Gulls on the posts, a heron in the shallows, the light changing slowly from grey to gold. {N} could stand here all morning without pressing anything at all.
- W | complain to the committee that the rival's winning print was edited | v: conformity | mark: made an enemy | closed: approval: accusing a fellow member; backfire: the complaint fails, and the club takes sides | chance: 50
- U | learn the manual settings one by one, until the camera stops guessing | v: achievement, self-direction | mark: learned a skill | self_control: + | chance: 70
- B | find where last year's winning shot was taken, and take it again, better | v: achievement, power | chance: 60
- R | climb down the harbour steps into the spray for the shot | body: heavy | v: stimulation | mark: took a wild risk | chance: 75
- G | walk the same lane every week and photograph the same tree through the year | habit | v: universalism (nature), tradition | chance: 60
- W>G | offer to photograph the village's oldest people for the history society | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 84
- U>W | teach the beginners' evening at the club, with handouts on exposure | binds | v: benevolence | chance: 64
- B>U | buy a widow's expensive lens second-hand, at half what it is worth | v: achievement, power | chance: 74
- R>B | enter the boldest picture you have, the one nobody else would dare | v: achievement, stimulation | chance: 60
- G>R | put the camera away and paddle along the shore with the gulls | v: hedonism | chance: 75
works: The print wins the month, and the judge holds it up and says it is the first picture of the evening that breathes.
works: {N} comes home with four hundred pictures and one, just one, that is exactly what they saw.
fails: Every shot of the morning is blurred, and the deadline comes and goes.
fails: The camera takes a wave full in the lens, and the screen goes dark for good.

